---
import { Mail } from '@lucide/astro';
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  locale="en"
  hasTranslation
  title="About"
  description="Hi, I'm Renjie, a software engineer who enjoys turning ideas into things people can use. Projects, small experiments, and notes on software, interaction, and intelligent applications."
>
  <div class="page-intro">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p><h1>Turning ideas into useful tools.</h1>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="about-layout container">
    <aside>
      <p class="about-lede">
        Hi, I'm Renjie, a software engineer who enjoys making things. For me,
        the pleasure of writing code is watching a vague idea become something
        people can use to solve a problem.
      </p>
      <p class="about-note">
        I explore software, interaction, and intelligent applications. I've
        worked on 3D creation tools and researched UAVs. Those experiences
        taught me to understand the problem first, test an idea, and keep
        refining it.
      </p>
      <p class="about-note">
        This site is home to my projects, small experiments, and thoughts along
        the way. Some come from work; others start with a question I want to
        understand. I hope they offer something useful to fellow curious people.
      </p>
      <div class="contact-links">
        <a class="button" href="mailto:renjie-l@foxmail.com"
          ><Mail size={16} /> Email</a
        >
      </div>
    </aside>
    <div class="about-content">
      <section class="interests">
        <p class="eyebrow">Interests</p><h2>What I care about</h2>
        <article>
          <h3>Making complex things easier to use</h3>
          <p>
            I'm interested in how people use tools: whether an interaction saves
            someone effort, or a reusable capability makes the next task easier.
            I've spent a lot of time on 3D creation, which keeps me thinking
            about both how software works and how it feels to use.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Working with new tools</h3>
          <p>
            Lately, I've been exploring how AI can help with real software
            projects: understanding a codebase, trying ideas, and checking
            results, while considering which decisions I need to make myself. I
            like starting with a concrete problem and seeing where a tool helps.
          </p>
        </article>
      </section>
      <section>
        <p class="eyebrow">Things I've built</p><h2>A few explorations</h2>
        <div class="work-grid">
          <article class="detail-card">
            <span>From work</span><h3>Building tools for 3D creation</h3>
            <p>
              At work, I've brought scene editing, asset generation, and image
              output into a shared creative workflow. It made me think more
              carefully about how a tool's capabilities fit together and how a
              complex system can keep evolving.
            </p>
            <a
              class="text-link"
              href="/projects/3d-creation-platform"
              hreflang="zh-CN">Anonymous case study (中文) →</a
            >
          </article>
          <article class="detail-card">
            <span>From research to flight</span><h3>
              Testing ideas in the real world
            </h3>
            <p>
              During graduate school, I studied how to reduce the swing of loads
              carried by a UAV. Moving from simulation to a physical flight
              platform taught me to respect the limits of a model and test ideas
              through experiments.
            </p>
            <a
              class="text-link"
              href="/projects/uav-swing-free-trajectory"
              hreflang="zh-CN">Research and experiments (中文) →</a
            >
          </article>
          <article class="detail-card">
            <span>Personal experiment</span><h3>
              Exploring 3D scenes in the browser
            </h3>
            <p>
              I also built an interactive Gaussian splat scene viewer to try the
              technology on its own. A small experiment doesn't have to become a
              full product to be worth documenting and sharing.
            </p>
            <a
              class="text-link"
              href="/projects/gaussian-splat-viewer"
              hreflang="zh-CN">Experiment notes (中文) →</a
            >
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section>
        <p class="eyebrow">Background</p><h2>Background</h2>
        <div class="background-sections">
          <section>
            <p class="eyebrow">Work</p><h3>Work experience</h3><div
              class="timeline"
            >
              <article>
                <span>2024.10 — Present</span><h4>
                  Large-scale 3D Design & Content Platform
                </h4><p>
                  Senior Software Development Engineer · Technical Lead for Web
                  3D and Real-time Rendering
                </p>
              </article><article>
                <span>2023.04 — 2024.10</span><h4>
                  Large-scale 3D Design & Content Platform
                </h4><p>
                  Software Development Engineer · Core Frontend Engineer for
                  Cloud and Real-time Rendering
                </p>
              </article>
            </div>
          </section>
          <section>
            <p class="eyebrow">Education</p><h3>Education</h3><div
              class="timeline"
            >
              <article>
                <span>2020.09 — 2023.06</span><h4>
                  Hangzhou Dianzi University
                </h4><p>M.Eng. · Electronic Information</p>
              </article><article>
                <span>2020.09 — 2022.06</span><h4>ITMO University</h4><p>
                  Master · Control Engineering
                </p>
              </article>
            </div>
          </section>
          <section>
            <p class="eyebrow">Publication</p><h3>Publication</h3><a
              class="publication publication-link"
              href="https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/abstract/document/10055333"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >
              First author · Deep Reinforcement Learning-based Swing-Free
              Trajectories Planning Algorithm for UAV with a Suspended Load. <em
                >China Automation Congress 2022.</em
              >
            </a>
          </section>
          <section>
            <p class="eyebrow">Awards</p><h3>Awards</h3><ul class="awards">
              <li>
                <time>2022</time>Silver Award, Zhejiang “Internet+” Innovation
                and Entrepreneurship Competition
              </li><li>
                <time>2021</time>First Prize, East China Division, China
                Graduate Electronics Design Contest
              </li><li>
                <time>2021</time>China Scholarship Council sponsored-study
                qualification
              </li><li>
                <time>2020</time>Graduate Academic Scholarship
              </li>
            </ul>
          </section>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(260px, 0.75fr) minmax(0, 1.25fr);
    gap: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 8rem);
    padding-top: 4rem;
  }
  aside {
    align-self: start;
    position: sticky;
    top: 7rem;
  }
  .about-lede {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .about-note {
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin: 1.2rem 0 0;
  }
  .contact-links {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .about-content {
    display: grid;
    gap: 4.5rem;
  }
  section h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1.3rem;
    font-size: 1.45rem;
  }
  .interests article + article {
    margin-top: 1.8rem;
  }
  .interests h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }
  .interests p:not(.eyebrow) {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }
  .background-sections {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  .background-sections section > h3 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }
  .timeline {
    border-left: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.8rem;
  }
  .timeline article {
    position: relative;
  }
  .timeline article::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: calc(-1.5rem - 4px);
    top: 0.5rem;
    width: 7px;
    height: 7px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent);
  }
  .timeline span,
  .detail-card > span {
    color: var(--accent);
    font:
      600 0.75rem ui-monospace,
      monospace;
  }
  .timeline h4,
  .detail-card h3 {
    margin: 0.3rem 0;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }
  .timeline p,
  .detail-card p,
  .publication {
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .detail-card {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: var(--surface);
  }
  .work-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .work-grid .detail-card p {
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  .detail-card .text-link {
    margin-top: 0.8rem;
    white-space: normal;
  }
  .publication-link {
    display: block;
    line-height: 1.7;
    transition: color 160ms ease;
  }
  .publication-link:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .awards {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
  }
  .awards li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 60px 1fr;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.8rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .awards time {
    color: var(--muted);
    font:
      0.82rem ui-monospace,
      monospace;
  }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .about-layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    aside {
      position: static;
    }
  }
</style>
